---
/** Help: search syntax, filters, keyboard shortcuts, sound, citing, playlists. */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { hasCleanAudio } from "../../lib/site-data.ts";

const sound = hasCleanAudio();
---

<Base
  title="Help"
  description="How to search, filter, cite and make playlists, and the keyboard shortcuts."
>
  <div class="wrap page help">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Help</h1>
      <nav class="btn-row" aria-label="On this page">
        <a class="chip" href="#search">
          Searching
        </a>
        <a class="chip" href="#filters">
          Filters
        </a>
        <a class="chip" href="#keys">
          Keyboard
        </a>
        {sound && (
          <a class="chip" href="#sound">
            Sound
          </a>
        )}
        <a class="chip" href="#cite">
          Citing
        </a>
        <a class="chip" href="#playlists">
          Playlists
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>
    <div class="reading">
      <h2 id="search">Searching</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Words are combined: <code>king ring seder</code> finds recordings with all three words.
        </li>
        <li>
          Put a phrase in quotes for an exact match: <code>"ad mosai"</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          The last word matches as a prefix: <code>hachn</code> finds <em>hachnasas orchim</em>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Excluding a word (<code>-word</code>), OR and NOT are not supported yet.
        </li>
        <li>
          As you type, the box suggests people, midos, mitzvos, Yom Tov, parshiyos, sources, places,
          serials and episode numbers (<code>ep 271</code>). Choosing one sets a filter, which also
          finds recordings whose transcript spells the word differently.
        </li>
        <li>
          Search covers titles, summaries, lessons, keywords and the automatic transcripts. A result
          found only in the transcript says so and shows the passages, each with a time you can jump
          to. Hebrew-script words search the Yiddish recordings, which show the time of the match
          but no text.
        </li>
        <li>
          Spelling varies (Dayeinu, Dayenu): when a transcript search finds little, a few common
          spelling variants are tried and listed.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="filters">Filters</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Different filters combine with AND; several values in one filter combine with OR. Filters
          marked <em>any | all</em> can require every ticked value.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every value can be excluded with its “not” button (or <kbd>x</kbd> on a focused value).
          Excluded values are struck through.
        </li>
        <li>
          “Leave out stories with…” removes recordings that carry a parents' note on that theme.
        </li>
        <li>The number beside each value is how many results you would get by ticking it.</li>
        <li>Everything is in the address bar: copy the link to share the exact search.</li>
        <li>
          “Suitable from age” is the youngest age a recording suits; 3 to 6 finds recordings for
          young children.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="keys">Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <p>
        Single-key shortcuts never fire while you are typing, and can be switched off in the
        shortcuts panel (<kbd>?</kbd>).
      </p>
      <table class="data">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>/</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Focus search</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>j</kbd> / <kbd>k</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Next / previous search result</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>Enter</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Open the focused result</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>p</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Play the focused result</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>a</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Add the focused result (or this recording) to a playlist</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>f</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Focus the filters</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>x</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Exclude the focused filter value</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>Space</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Play / pause</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Back 15 seconds / forward 30 seconds</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>[</kbd> / <kbd>]</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Previous / next chapter</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>&lt;</kbd> / <kbd>&gt;</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Slower / faster</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>c</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Copy a link to this recording at the current time</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>t</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Jump to the transcript</td>
          </tr>
          {sound && (
            <tr>
              <td>
                <kbd>s</kbd>
              </td>
              <td>Switch between the original and the AI-improved sound</td>
            </tr>
          )}
          <tr>
            <td>
              <kbd>?</kbd>
            </td>
            <td>Show the shortcuts</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      {sound && (
        <>
          <h2 id="sound">Sound: original and AI-improved</h2>
          <p>
            The player plays the original tape by default. Under <strong>Sound</strong> in the
            player bar you can switch to an <strong>AI-improved</strong> copy, cleaned by a
            speech-restoration model: less hiss, clearer voices, but sometimes a slightly synthetic
            voice, and songs or music may be garbled. Switching keeps your place, so you can compare
            the two by switching back and forth (shortcut: <kbd>s</kbd>). The setting is remembered
            in this browser, for this site only. Both copies have the same length, so timestamps,
            transcript links and citations work with either. Some recordings may not have an
            AI-improved copy yet; for those the original plays and the player says so. The
            AI-improved files are about a third larger.
          </p>
        </>
      )}

      <h2 id="cite">Citing</h2>
      <p>
        “Cite” on a recording gives a short form, a full form and a link. If the player is past the
        first few seconds, or you opened the page at a time, the time is included and the link opens
        the recording there. You can also select words in the transcript and copy them as a quote
        with its citation. Links take <code>?t=754</code>, <code>?t=12m34s</code> or
        <code>?t=12:34</code>; the page opens at that time without starting to play.
      </p>

      <h2 id="playlists">Playlists</h2>
      <p>
        “+ Playlist” adds a recording, or just one chapter or serial chapter, to a playlist of your
        own. Playlists are saved in this browser only: there are no accounts, and clearing browser
        data, a private window or another device will not have them. Export a file to back up or
        share; import it on any device. Short playlists can also be shared as a link.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .help h2 {
    margin-top: 1.5em;
    scroll-margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .help ul li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .help table {
    max-width: 560px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
  }
</style>
